1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:02,140
Your assignment is finished.

2
00:00:02,140 --> 00:00:08,190
PackCheck helps you prepare the submission ZIP with the required filenames and folder

3
00:00:08,190 --> 00:00:08,900
structure.

4
00:00:09,150 --> 00:00:14,490
This fictional assignment requires a report, README, and source folder.

5
00:00:14,490 --> 00:00:19,000
The laptop has different filenames and an extra system file.

6
00:00:19,250 --> 00:00:23,080
I load the fictional example in the working prototype.

7
00:00:23,080 --> 00:00:27,540
You can import your own files through pickers or drag and drop.

8
00:00:27,790 --> 00:00:34,340
Requirements use exact paths, one per line. Missing paths appear immediately.

9
00:00:34,340 --> 00:00:38,340
Blocking issues keep the Build button disabled.

10
00:00:38,590 --> 00:00:42,250
I select the report and apply its required path.

11
00:00:42,250 --> 00:00:47,360
The original stays unchanged, with its filename visible underneath.

12
00:00:47,610 --> 00:00:53,300
Next, I apply the README path. This changes its place in the ZIP.

13
00:00:53,300 --> 00:00:56,450
The contents still need your review.

14
00:00:56,700 --> 00:01:04,770
The preview lets me read the README before packing. Text stays plain text, including HTML.

15
00:01:04,770 --> 00:01:07,200
Images also have a preview.

16
00:01:07,450 --> 00:01:10,230
I deliberately create a duplicate path.

17
00:01:10,230 --> 00:01:16,650
PackCheck blocks building, preventing one file from silently replacing another in the ZIP.

18
00:01:16,900 --> 00:01:20,670
Restoring the README path clears the conflict.

19
00:01:20,670 --> 00:01:24,520
You can edit paths directly and undo a removal.

20
00:01:24,770 --> 00:01:29,870
System metadata stays excluded by default and visible for review.

21
00:01:29,870 --> 00:01:33,320
Your selected files keep their folder paths.

22
00:01:33,570 --> 00:01:38,760
I add an outer folder here. All selected files go inside it.

23
00:01:38,760 --> 00:01:42,920
Requirements still describe the contents within.

24
00:01:43,170 --> 00:01:45,700
A local worker builds the ZIP.

25
00:01:45,700 --> 00:01:52,970
PackCheck reopens it, compares every file byte, and checks the actual compressed size.

26
00:01:53,220 --> 00:01:54,540
I build the ZIP.

27
00:01:54,540 --> 00:02:01,970
The result shows its actual size and file count, confirming its contents match the inputs.

28
00:02:02,220 --> 00:02:06,390
This downloads the ZIP with our chosen outer folder.

29
00:02:06,390 --> 00:02:10,970
Review the package, then upload it to your course portal.

30
00:02:11,220 --> 00:02:14,650
The file list downloads separately for review.

31
00:02:14,650 --> 00:02:20,390
It stays outside the assignment ZIP, which only contains your selected files.

32
00:02:20,640 --> 00:02:25,070
Switching to Chinese preserves the settings and generated ZIP.

33
00:02:25,070 --> 00:02:29,560
Smaller screens get an adapted layout and a packaging shortcut.

34
00:02:29,810 --> 00:02:33,140
Files stay in this tab and clear on refresh.

35
00:02:33,140 --> 00:02:38,290
You remain responsible for assignment contents and final submission.

36
00:02:38,540 --> 00:02:44,070
PackCheck is available now, with source on GitHub. Try your files.

37
00:02:44,070 --> 00:02:48,680
Next, we will test it against real student assignments.
